---
// All three calculators, with one script that wires up whichever is on the page.
// Astro hoists and bundles every <script> in a component into the pages that
// render it, so a per-tool script would still load on the other two tools and
// throw on missing elements. One script that checks for its own inputs first is
// the version that survives that.
//
// Nothing here accepts a body weight, an age or a condition, and nothing
// returns a dose. Each tool states its formula above the inputs, so the
// arithmetic can be checked by hand.
import { DEFAULT_SYRINGE_ML } from '../lib/reconstitution';

interface Props {
  slug: string;
  /** The reconstitution tool's section id and heading, overridable so the same
   *  component can sit inside a compound page under that page's own H2. */
  id?: string;
  heading?: string;
  headingLevel?: 2 | 3;
}
const { slug, id = 'calc-recon', heading = 'Work out concentration and what to draw', headingLevel = 2 } = Astro.props;
const H = headingLevel === 3 ? 'h3' : 'h2';
---
{slug === 'reconstitution-calculator' && (
  <section id={id}>
    <H>{heading}</H>
    <p class="prose">Two divisions, both shown. <b>Concentration</b> = mass in the vial &divide; diluent volume. <b>Volume to draw</b> = mass you want &divide; that concentration. Syringe capacity sets how much fits, and the scale sets how many units each millilitre represents.</p>
    <form class="calc" onsubmit="return false">
      <label for="r-mass">Mass in vial (mg)</label>
      <input id="r-mass" type="number" step="any" min="0" inputmode="decimal" value="5" />
      <label for="r-vol">Diluent added (mL)</label>
      <input id="r-vol" type="number" step="any" min="0" inputmode="decimal" value="2" />
      <label for="r-want">Mass per draw</label>
      <div class="draw-mass">
        <input id="r-want" type="number" step="any" min="0" inputmode="decimal" value="250" aria-describedby="r-current-unit" />
        <span id="r-current-unit" hidden>Micrograms</span>
        <fieldset class="mass-units" aria-label="Mass per draw unit">
          <input id="r-unit-mcg" type="radio" name="r-unit" value="mcg" checked />
          <label for="r-unit-mcg">mcg</label>
          <input id="r-unit-mg" type="radio" name="r-unit" value="mg" />
          <label for="r-unit-mg">mg</label>
        </fieldset>
      </div>
      <label for="r-scale">Syringe scale</label>
      <select id="r-scale" class="draw-select">
        <option value="100" selected>U-100 (100 units per mL)</option>
        <option value="50">U-50 (50 units per mL)</option>
        <option value="40">U-40 (40 units per mL)</option>
      </select>
      <label for="r-capacity">Syringe capacity</label>
      <select id="r-capacity" class="draw-select">
        {[0.3, 0.5, DEFAULT_SYRINGE_ML].map((capacity) => (
          <option value={capacity} selected={capacity === DEFAULT_SYRINGE_ML}>{capacity} mL</option>
        ))}
      </select>
      <output id="r-out" class="draw-result" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true" hidden>
        <span id="r-message" hidden></span>
        <span id="r-summary" hidden>
          <span class="draw-kicker">Volume to draw</span>
          <span id="r-volume" class="draw-volume"></span>
          <span id="r-reading" class="draw-reading"></span>
          <span class="capacity-gauge" aria-hidden="true">
            <span class="gauge-label">Syringe fill</span>
            <span class="gauge-track"><span id="r-fill" class="gauge-fill"></span></span>
            <span class="gauge-labels"><span>0</span><span id="r-gauge-max"></span></span>
          </span>
          <span class="draw-details">
            <span>Concentration<span id="r-concentration" class="draw-detail-value"></span></span>
            <span>Whole draws per vial<span id="r-count" class="draw-detail-value"></span></span>
          </span>
          <span id="r-small-draw" class="draw-note" hidden>Below 1 syringe unit. Check the smallest graduation on your syringe.</span>
        </span>
      </output>
    </form>
    <p class="prose">Worked example: 5&nbsp;mg in 2&nbsp;mL is 2,500&nbsp;mcg/mL, so 250&nbsp;mcg is 0.1&nbsp;mL, which is 10&nbsp;units on a U-100 syringe and 4&nbsp;units on a U-40. The scale is printed on the barrel; reading a U-40 syringe as if it were U-100 is a two-and-a-half-fold error.</p>
  </section>
)}

{slug === 'unit-converter' && (
  <section id="calc-convert">
    <h2>Convert a mass, or a volume to syringe units</h2>
    <p class="prose">Mass conversions are fixed ratios: 1&nbsp;mg = 1,000&nbsp;mcg = 1,000,000&nbsp;ng. Volume to units depends only on the scale printed on your syringe.</p>
    <form class="calc" onsubmit="return false">
      <label for="c-amount">Amount</label>
      <input id="c-amount" type="number" step="any" min="0" inputmode="decimal" value="250" />
      <label for="c-from">From</label>
      <select id="c-from">
        <option value="mg">mg (milligrams)</option>
        <option value="mcg" selected>mcg (micrograms)</option>
        <option value="ng">ng (nanograms)</option>
        <option value="ml">mL (millilitres)</option>
      </select>
      <label for="c-scale">Syringe scale, for volume conversions</label>
      <select id="c-scale">
        <option value="100" selected>U-100 (100 units per mL)</option>
        <option value="50">U-50 (50 units per mL)</option>
        <option value="40">U-40 (40 units per mL)</option>
      </select>
      <output id="c-out" aria-live="polite"></output>
    </form>
    <h3>Why there is no IU box</h3>
    <p class="prose">International units are not a mass. An IU is defined separately for each substance by an international reference preparation, so the number of micrograms in one IU is different for every compound and exists only where someone has published a factor. There is no general formula, and a converter that offers one is inventing it.</p>
    <p class="prose">If you have a published factor for a specific compound, the arithmetic is one multiplication you can do here: enter the mass in micrograms that the factor gives for one IU, and read the total. This tool will not supply that factor, because supplying it for a compound that has none is exactly the error it exists to avoid.</p>
  </section>
)}

{slug === 'vial-planner' && (
  <section id="calc-vial">
    <h2>How far a vial goes</h2>
    <p class="prose"><b>Draws per vial</b> = total mass in the vial &divide; mass per draw, rounded down, because a partial draw is not a draw. How long that lasts is that count &divide; how often you draw.</p>
    <form class="calc" onsubmit="return false">
      <label for="v-mass">Mass in vial (mg)</label>
      <input id="v-mass" type="number" step="any" min="0" inputmode="decimal" value="5" />
      <label for="v-vol">Diluent added (mL)</label>
      <input id="v-vol" type="number" step="any" min="0" inputmode="decimal" value="2" />
      <label for="v-want">Mass per draw (mcg)</label>
      <input id="v-want" type="number" step="any" min="0" inputmode="decimal" value="250" />
      <label for="v-freq">Draws per week</label>
      <input id="v-freq" type="number" step="any" min="0" inputmode="decimal" value="7" />
      <output id="v-out" aria-live="polite"></output>
    </form>
    <p class="prose">The leftover matters. A vial that yields 20.4 draws yields 20, and the remainder is the fraction you cannot measure, not a bonus draw. A requested mass above the vial total yields zero whole draws. This tool will not tell you what mass to draw; that is the number a study reported or a clinician set, and it is the one input it refuses to guess.</p>
  </section>
)}

<script>
  import { calculateDraw, DEFAULT_SYRINGE_ML } from '../lib/reconstitution';

  const num = (id: string): number => {
    const el = document.getElementById(id) as HTMLInputElement | null;
    return el ? parseFloat(el.value) : NaN;
  };
  const pick = (id: string): string => {
    const el = document.getElementById(id) as HTMLSelectElement | null;
    return el ? el.value : '';
  };
  const round = (n: number, dp = 3): string =>
    n.toLocaleString('en-US', { maximumFractionDigits: dp });

  /** Wires inputs to a render function, runs it once, and skips the tool entirely
   *  when its output element is not on this page. */
  function wire(outId: string, ids: string[], render: (out: HTMLElement) => void) {
    const out = document.getElementById(outId);
    if (!out) return;
    const run = () => render(out);
    ids.forEach((id) => document.getElementById(id)?.addEventListener('input', run));
    ids.forEach((id) => document.getElementById(id)?.addEventListener('change', run));
    run();
  }

  function setupDrawCalculator() {
    const byId = (id: string) => document.getElementById(id)!;
    const amount = document.getElementById('r-want') as HTMLInputElement | null;
    if (!amount) return;

    const mgUnit = byId('r-unit-mg') as HTMLInputElement;
    const currentUnit = byId('r-current-unit');
    const message = byId('r-message');
    const summary = byId('r-summary');
    const volume = byId('r-volume');
    const reading = byId('r-reading');
    const fill = byId('r-fill');
    const gaugeMax = byId('r-gauge-max');
    const concentration = byId('r-concentration');
    const count = byId('r-count');
    const smallDraw = byId('r-small-draw');
    let wasMg = mgUnit.checked;

    // Shift the entered decimal's exponent to avoid changing a boundary value
    // by a floating-point digit when switching units.
    const shift = (value: string, places: number) => {
      const [digits, exponent = '0'] = value.split(/[eE]/);
      return Number(`${digits}e${Number(exponent) + places}`);
    };
    const positiveLabel = (value: number, minimum: number, decimals: number) =>
      value < minimum ? `<${minimum}` : round(value, decimals);

    wire('r-out', ['r-mass', 'r-vol', 'r-want', 'r-unit-mcg', 'r-unit-mg', 'r-scale', 'r-capacity'], (out) => {
      const isMg = mgUnit.checked;
      if (isMg !== wasMg) {
        if (amount.value !== '') {
          const converted = shift(amount.value, isMg ? -3 : 3);
          if (Number.isFinite(converted) && converted !== 0) amount.value = String(converted);
          else if (Number(amount.value) !== 0) amount.value = '';
        }
        wasMg = isMg;
      }
      currentUnit.textContent = isMg ? 'Milligrams' : 'Micrograms';

      const capacity = num('r-capacity');
      const scale = num('r-scale');
      const mcg = isMg ? shift(amount.value, 3) : num('r-want');
      const result = calculateDraw(num('r-mass'), num('r-vol'), mcg, scale, capacity);
      out.hidden = false;
      summary.hidden = result.status !== 'ok';
      message.hidden = result.status === 'ok';

      if (result.status === 'invalid') {
        message.textContent = 'Enter a positive number for the vial, the diluent and the mass per draw.';
      } else if (result.status === 'over-vial') {
        message.textContent = 'The requested mass exceeds the total mass in the vial.';
      } else if (result.status === 'over-syringe') {
        message.textContent = `The calculated draw volume exceeds a ${capacity} mL syringe.`;
      } else {
        const { concentration: conc, drawMl, units, draws } = result;
        volume.textContent = `${positiveLabel(drawMl, 0.001, 3)} mL`;
        reading.textContent = `${positiveLabel(units, 0.01, 2)} units on a U-${scale} syringe`;
        fill.style.width = `${Math.min(100, (drawMl / capacity) * 100)}%`;
        gaugeMax.textContent = `${capacity} mL`;
        concentration.textContent = `${positiveLabel(conc, 0.1, 1)} mcg/mL (${positiveLabel(conc / 1000, 0.001, 3)} mg/mL)`;
        count.textContent = round(draws, 0);
        smallDraw.hidden = units >= 1;
      }
    });
  }

  setupDrawCalculator();

  // Unit converter: fixed mass ratios, plus volume to syringe units.
  wire('c-out', ['c-amount', 'c-from', 'c-scale'], (out) => {
    const amount = num('c-amount');
    const from = pick('c-from');
    const perMl = parseFloat(pick('c-scale')) || 100;
    if (!(amount >= 0) || Number.isNaN(amount)) {
      out.textContent = 'Enter a number to convert.';
      return;
    }
    if (from === 'ml') {
      out.textContent = `${round(amount, 3)} mL = ${round(amount * perMl, 1)} units on a U-${perMl} syringe`;
      return;
    }
    const toMcg: Record<string, number> = { mg: 1000, mcg: 1, ng: 0.001 };
    const mcg = amount * (toMcg[from] ?? 1);
    out.textContent = [
      `${round(mcg / 1000, 6)} mg`,
      `${round(mcg, 3)} mcg`,
      `${round(mcg * 1000, 0)} ng`,
    ].join(' · ');
  });

  // Vial planner: whole draws, how long they last, and the unusable remainder.
  wire('v-out', ['v-mass', 'v-vol', 'v-want', 'v-freq'], (out) => {
    const mg = num('v-mass'), ml = num('v-vol'), mcg = num('v-want'), freq = num('v-freq');
    if (!(mg > 0 && mcg > 0)) {
      out.textContent = 'Enter a positive vial mass and mass per draw.';
      return;
    }
    const totalMcg = mg * 1000;
    if (mcg > totalMcg) {
      out.textContent = 'Whole draws per vial: 0. The requested mass exceeds the total mass in the vial.';
      return;
    }
    const draws = Math.floor(totalMcg / mcg);
    const leftoverMcg = totalMcg - draws * mcg;
    const lines = [`Whole draws per vial: ${draws}`];
    if (ml > 0) {
      const conc = totalMcg / ml;
      lines.push(`Each draw: ${round(mcg / conc, 3)} mL`);
      lines.push(`Left in the vial: ${round(leftoverMcg, 1)} mcg (${round(leftoverMcg / conc, 3)} mL)`);
    } else {
      lines.push(`Left over: ${round(leftoverMcg, 1)} mcg`);
    }
    if (freq > 0) {
      const weeks = draws / freq;
      lines.push(`At ${round(freq, 2)} draws per week: ${round(weeks, 2)} weeks (${round(weeks * 7, 1)} days)`);
    }
    out.textContent = lines.join(' · ');
  });
</script>

<style>
  .draw-mass { display: flex; align-items: stretch; gap: .45rem; max-width: 18rem; }
  .draw-mass #r-want { flex: 1; min-width: 0; }
  .mass-units {
    position: relative; display: flex; flex: none; align-items: stretch;
    margin: 0; padding: 2px; border: 1px solid var(--rule); border-radius: 5px;
    background: var(--paper);
  }
  .mass-units input {
    position: absolute; inline-size: 1px; block-size: 1px; padding: 0;
    clip-path: inset(50%); overflow: hidden; white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .mass-units label {
    display: grid; place-items: center; min-inline-size: 2.65rem; padding: .16rem .3rem;
    margin: 0; border: 1px solid transparent; border-radius: 3px; cursor: pointer;
  }
  .mass-units input:checked + label {
    color: var(--accent); border-color: var(--accent); font-weight: 650;
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 10%, var(--paper));
  }
  .mass-units input:focus-visible + label { outline: 2px solid var(--accent); outline-offset: 2px; }
  .draw-select {
    max-width: 100%; font: inherit; padding: .3rem .45rem; border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    border-radius: 4px; background: var(--paper); color: var(--ink);
  }
  .calc .draw-result {
    padding: .9rem 1rem; border: 1px solid var(--rule); border-radius: 6px;
    background: var(--paper); color: var(--ink); font-family: var(--sans);
  }
  .calc .draw-result[hidden], .draw-result [hidden] { display: none; }
  .draw-kicker, .draw-volume, .draw-reading, .gauge-label, .draw-detail-value { display: block; }
  .draw-kicker, .gauge-label, .gauge-labels, .draw-details { font-size: .875rem; color: var(--ink-2); }
  .draw-volume {
    font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 5vw, 2.5rem); line-height: 1.2; font-weight: 700;
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }
  .draw-reading { font-size: .95rem; color: var(--ink-2); }
  .capacity-gauge { display: block; margin-top: .85rem; }
  .gauge-track {
    position: relative; display: block; height: .85rem; margin-top: .28rem;
    overflow: hidden; border: 1px solid var(--rule); border-radius: 3px; background: var(--surface);
  }
  .gauge-fill { display: block; height: 100%; width: 0; background: var(--accent); }
  .gauge-track::after {
    content: ''; position: absolute; inset: 0; pointer-events: none;
    background: repeating-linear-gradient(to right, transparent 0 calc(10% - 1px), color-mix(in srgb, var(--ink) 38%, transparent) calc(10% - 1px) 10%);
  }
  .gauge-labels { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; margin-top: .15rem; }
  .draw-details {
    display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: .55rem 1.4rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); margin-top: .65rem; padding-top: .65rem;
  }
  .draw-detail-value { color: var(--ink); overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  .draw-note { display: block; margin-top: .65rem; font-size: .875rem; }
</style>
